10. Content & Compliance Guidelines

Because this website relates to medical education and international admissions, accuracy and transparency are essential.

Verify university recognition and accreditation information using current official sources.

Ensure country-specific admission details are accurate.

Verify applicable NEET and National Medical Commission requirements.

Do not guarantee admission, visa approval, scholarships, licensing, or future employment.

Do not describe every foreign medical university as automatically suitable for Indian students.

Explain the importance of checking course structure, internship arrangements, medium of instruction, and applicable registration requirements.

Display clear disclaimers wherever necessary.

Keep tuition fees and living costs updated.

Do not publish fabricated student testimonials or university partnerships.

The website should position the consultancy as a responsible admission guidance provider, not as an authority that can guarantee university or government decisions.

